  "privacyTitle": "Privacy",
  "privacyIntro": "Companion holds one kind of data: what you typed about your animals. This page says where it sits and what can take it off this phone.",
  "privacyStoredHeading": "What is stored",
  "privacyStoredBody": "Every animal, dose, weigh-in, screening, visit, symptom, handover and buyer contact — and the photographs you attached — in a database and a picture folder inside this app's private storage. Android keeps that folder out of reach of other apps, and the files are not encrypted beyond that.",
  "privacyBackupHeading": "What leaves this phone",
  "privacyBackupBody": "Only what you export: a ZIP with every record and picture, a CSV of one table, or a PDF of one animal. Each goes wherever you send it, so a backup carries your buyers' names and phone numbers — treat the file the way you would the paper it replaces. Turn on the app lock if the phone travels.",
  "privacyCollectHeading": "What is collected about you",
  "privacyCollectBody": "Nothing. There is no analytics, no crash reporting, no advertising identifier and no network call in this app.",
  "privacyRemoveHeading": "How to erase it",
  "privacyRemoveBody": "Uninstalling removes the database and the picture folder with it. There is no copy anywhere else, so export a pack first if the records matter — and remember that the app lock's PIN cannot be recovered either.",
  "termsTitle": "Terms of use",
  "termsUseHeading": "What this app is for",
  "termsUseBody": "Keeping your own records about the animals in your care. One licence per person; install it on the phones you use.",
  "termsDataHeading": "Your data is yours",
  "termsDataBody": "We hold no copy of it and cannot restore it. Backups are your responsibility, and the export tile in Settings is the whole mechanism.",
  "termsAdviceHeading": "Not veterinary advice",
  "termsAdviceBody": "Companion repeats what you typed and applies arithmetic to dates and weights. It does not diagnose, and a reminder is a calendar entry, not a clinical opinion. Call a veterinarian.",
  "termsWarrantyHeading": "No warranty",
  "termsWarrantyBody": "The app is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, no liability is accepted for a lost record, a missed reminder or a decision taken on what is written here.",
  "helpTitle": "Help",
  "helpQ1": "How do I back up?",
  "helpA1": "Settings, then Export records. The ZIP file carries every row and every picture; send it to yourself and keep it. Restoring reads the same file back on any phone.",
  "helpQ2": "I forgot my PIN",
  "helpA2": "It cannot be recovered, because only a hash of it is stored. Uninstalling the app clears the lock and the ledger with it, so if you have a recent pack, restore that afterwards.",
  "helpQ3": "I lost my phone",
  "helpA3": "Nothing is on a server, so nothing can be sent back. A pack you exported earlier restores the ledger on a new phone; one you never exported is gone.",
  "helpQ4": "Where do the reminders come from?",
  "helpA4": "From the next-due dates you typed. Companion books an alarm a month ahead and one on the morning itself; if notifications are switched off for the app, the dates still show in the herd's agenda.",
  "helpQ5": "Why does a picture say it is not on this phone?",
  "helpA5": "The row survived and the file did not — usually after a restore from a pack that carried no pictures. Adding the photo again fixes it.",
  "helpQ6": "Can I hand over the animal's record?",
  "helpA6": "Yes. Open the animal and export its PDF: a fixed document the buyer can keep without this app. The handover itself is recorded on the same page.",
  "helpQ7": "Which languages are there?",
  "helpA7": "English, Arabic, French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese and Dutch. Settings, then Language — the change applies immediately.",
  "helpQ8": "Something is wrong with the app",
  "helpA8": "Write to us and say what you were doing when it happened. The version is on the About page.",
  "helpContactHeading": "Write to us",
  "whatsNewTitle": "What's new",
  "whatsNew1": "Photographs on the herd cards, and a warmer, roomier layout throughout.",
